WEBVTT

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.510
Being Here

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.760
So let's do an experiment.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.390
Finest Quality Refined Rice Flour
Domestic Wet-land Glutinous Rice 100%

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.520
Should we start with 200 grams
for the sticky rice flour dumplings?

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.770
Yeah!

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:45.600
NOD

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.190
Should we call it
"chilled shiratama syrup"?

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.230
Yeah, that's really cute!

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:56.950
<i>Crescent Moon was going to have a food stand
at the annual summer festival</i>

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.240
<i>in the shopping district.</i>

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.870
<i>This year, Grandpa let us decide
what would be on the menu.</i>

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.870
March Town Shopping District
March Town Festival
Sunday, July 28th

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:08.960
To explain it simply,
the way you make rice flour dumplings...

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.960
Step one. Knead the rice flour in cold water.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.340
Step two. Roll into balls and boil in hot water.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.840
That's all.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.470
GIGGLE

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.470
AHAHA

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.470
See? Simple, right?

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:23.520
What? "Simple, right?" It's way too simple!

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.520
EHHH

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.770
I think we'll go with 200 grams of rice flour
and about 160 cc of cold water.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.770
Rice flour is sold
at the super market.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.780
Put the flour in a bowl and pour the water in
a little at a time, mixing as we go.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.570
Once it's mixed well,
put some muscle in it as you knead it.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.950
If you put in too much water, it'll get sticky,
and make it hard to form into balls,

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.160
so stop when the dough has taken shape.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.830
Then roll the dough out
into rod shapes with your hands

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.130
and rip them apart into bite-sized piece.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.760
I'm getting the hang of it!

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.880
KNEAD
KNEAD

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.880
ROLL
ROLL

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.510
This is fun!

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.140
Rice flour dumplings! This is Momo's!

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.300
FWHAAA

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.720
PUSH
PUSH

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:03.720
SQUISH
SQUISH

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.100
Yes, you're doing good, Momo.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.060
But maybe it's a little big.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.310
Sis, about this size?

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.560
Is it too small?

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.610
TINY

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.610
More circular?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:18.190
Don't worry. They'll expand a bit
when we boil them, so that's perfect.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:23.200
When making large rice flour dumplings,
you would put a little dent in them like this,

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.080
but today we're making smaller ones.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.540
Next we put them in boiling water.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.750
After two or three minutes,
they'll come burbling up to the surface.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.250
Maybe a little more.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.340
A little more?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.220
Then you keep them in the boiling water
for another minute.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.310
Then transfer them to ice water,
which firms them up.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.600
And...

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.140
They're done!

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.140
TA-DAA

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.560
Voila!

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.020
SPRINGY

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.060
Th-That was so fast! And simple!

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.230
Wonderful!

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.900
At first, let's just try it
with sugar and soy sauce.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.250
Yum!

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.460
It's so chewy!

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.380
The rice flour dumplings
pass the taste test,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.420
but the challenge is the syrup.

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.930
We have matcha, right?
Plum syrup, chilled sweet red bean soup...

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.640
It's so delicious with matcha!

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.220
But powdered matcha is expensive.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.350
I don't want to make each cup
more than 300 yen.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:39.940
Um, if we can get about 60 small dumplings
from 200 grams of rice flour...

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.900
Let's see...

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:42.950
HMMM

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:45.450
OH

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.280
I got it! How about cold milk tea?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.790
It's rich and sweet!

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.750
That could be good!

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.460
True, black tea leaves would be much cheaper!

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:59.800
Why don't we also put in black pearl tapioca?
It would make nice color accents!

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.510
That's a great idea!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.930
To defray the cost of the tapioca,
instead of using disposable bowls and spoons,

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:09.680
we can gather spoons and bowls from our house,
Crescent Moon, and Aunt Misaki's pub,

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.730
and just keep washing them,
even though it might be a hassle.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.600
- Oh, we can have Kiriyama do the washing!
- What?

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.690
Good idea! Let's ask him!

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.110
CRESCENT MOON

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.830
You did a pretty good job with the dumplings.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:35.580
You put them in ice water
to firm them up, right?

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:39.210
And tapioca?

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.550
Another fancy thing, huh?

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:47.090
Hey, it's pretty firm.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.100
This is a type of starch, right?

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:50.760
Grandpa.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:52.850
Wh-What do you think?

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:52.850
THUMP THUMP

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.980
Well, I guess it'll do.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.480
<i>Damn it, it's actually really good.</i>

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:02.480
I got a feeling the youngsters
will really like them.

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.320
It should sell pretty well at a food stand.
It's a festival, after all.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.330
BRIGHT

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.910
Yay!

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.660
This one was especially good.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.250
Plum syrup?

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.670
It's refreshing and tasty.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:21.460
That plum syrup was made by Chiho.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.800
Yeah? That's a nice smell from the plums.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.720
<i>As soon as summer vacation started,</i>

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:38.400
<i>we went to see Chiho.</i>

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.230
Chiho!

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:43.980
Hina.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.080
<i>She took me around the farm.</i>

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.080
WAG WAG WAG

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.580
WAHH

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.910
<i>Love!</i>

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.160
<i>Play with me. Woof-woof!</i>

00:06:58.330 --> 00:06:59.790
<i>Let's play!</i>

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:04.170
<i>She showed me Hana, and her puppies.</i>

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:07.420
<i>Love! I love you!</i>

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:20.770
<i>Sometimes while we talk,
Chiho would go silent and space out.</i>

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:33.200
<i>Ms. Satou said that even now, Chiho freezes up
when she sees a girl of middle school age.</i>

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:41.580
<i>Seeing someone of the same age
makes all of her painful memories</i>

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:46.250
<i>come flooding back into her heart and mind.</i>

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:53.640
<i>Apparently her body is resisting that
with every strength.</i>

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:00.060
<i>But Chiho is working hard here,</i>

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.060
<i>so that little by little,</i>

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:07.980
<i>she'll be able to talk
and act like she used to.</i>

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.070
<i>That's what Ms. Satou told me.</i>

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.950
CHIHO

00:08:12.530 --> 00:08:15.200
<i>Chiho developed a fever in the evening,</i>

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:19.700
<i>so her mom dropped Sis and me
off at the station.</i>

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:25.340
<i>"Thank you so much for supporting Chiho."</i>

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:30.340
<i>Her mom said that as she clasped my hands.</i>

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:35.260
<i>She said, "Chiho and I
will be doing our best here."</i>

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:47.520
<i>The first step is making friends with animals.</i>

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:51.190
<i>Next is making friends
with people older than you.</i>

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:56.530
<i>The third step is making friends
with people close to your age.</i>

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:07.420
<i>Even now, Chiho is fighting.</i>

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.760
<i>I'll send her photos from the summer festival.</i>

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:17.300
<i>Photos of everyone enjoying the plum syrup.</i>

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:23.020
<i>And then, I'll go visit her again.</i>

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.560
All right, shall we go?

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.230
Let's get started.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:31.480
CRESCENT MOON

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:36.610
Welcome! Crescent Moon here!

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.820
CRESCENT MOON

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.870
How about some sweet, chilled
rice flour dumpling syrup?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.870
Chilled
Rice Flour Dumpling Syrup
300 yen

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.870
Milk Tea
Plum Syrup
Sweet bean

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.120
Chilled Ginger Drink
100 yen

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:48.080
Sweet and cold rice flour dumpling syrup!

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.210
It's nice and cold!

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.590
Here's your plum syrup.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:58.720
Thank you.

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:01.510
It looks really good.

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.230
Here's some clean plates.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.350
And I'll take these back.

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.060
Thank you, Kiriyama!

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.690
PROMPT PROMPT

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.690
Also 100 yen coins.
I'll empty two rolls in here for change.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.990
PROMPT PROMPT

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.990
And dish cloths.
I'll hang up the ones I washed here.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.070
Kiriyama is the best! He's so considerate!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.490
That's a big help!

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.410
Sorry for working you so hard, kid.

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:25.080
Here, at least have a cool ginger drink.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.080
Thank you.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.960
There are so many people here.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:32.880
This is good.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:37.050
The festival is a success.
And we're selling like crazy too.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:43.430
This is my first time doing something
like this, so I'm kind of surprised.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.060
That it's pretty fun.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.140
Kiriyama! Kiriyama!

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:49.810
- Hey...
- What's up?

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:51.940
Yo. How you doing?

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.150
Takahashi.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:58.410
Huh? Have you gotten way taller again?

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:02.660
Chiho made this plum syrup.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.370
Thanks.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.410
<i>He's huge.</i>

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:07.790
WHOA

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:12.670
Grandma. Mikako.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:15.960
<i>Delicious three-colored
rice flour dumplings here!</i>

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.420
<i>Would you like any?</i>

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:19.340
<i>Welcome!</i>

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:24.930
It's all right. They're doing a great job.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:42.410
It's a nice night.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.660
Rei.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:50.920
This is what I like.

00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.720
I guess I love this kind of thing.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:07.680
Yeah.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:10.770
KA-CHING

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:12.020
STUFFED

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:17.030
TREMBLE
TREMBLE

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:17.030
Wow! It isn't even 7:00.
We made all this in no time at all!

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:23.870
At this rate, I think we can easily sell the curry
that's on the stove for dinner tonight!

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:25.530
S-Sis, calm down!

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:28.040
Curry is no good! We're a sweets shop!

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.210
Oh no, Sis!

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:35.000
We're down to less than one box of dumplings!
Even though we made a ton!

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.090
Let's boil some more right away!

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.550
We can't! We're out of syrup too!

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:40.880
EMPTY

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:43.890
What? Right when we're on a selling streak?

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:45.350
FWIP

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.100
Idiots!

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.100
SALESMAN

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:51.730
CRACKLE

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.390
We still have soybean flour
and brown sugar syrup, right?

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:51.730
G-Grandpa!

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:53.350
Akari, boil some water!

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:54.480
Right!

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:56.230
- Hina, mind the store!
- Okay!

00:12:56.230 --> 00:13:00.400
Kid, buy us some ice. Ask the Takahashi boy
and he'll tell you where.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:01.360
O-Okay!

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.780
I'll knead the dumplings!

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:07.530
All right! Kawamoto family, fight!

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:08.990
Yeah!

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:12.000
Being Here

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.000
Summer Vacation (Part 1)

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.760
CRESCENT MOON

00:13:21.420 --> 00:13:25.090
The March Town Festival was so much fun.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:26.470
COZY

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.890
We should've prepared more syrup, huh?

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:36.690
I never thought we'd sell out by 7:00.
Such a shame.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.650
Speaking of shame, you spent too much on it
and were too generous with the portions.

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:43.860
After working so hard drenched in sweat,
this is our net profit.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:46.990
This is what they call
"going through great pains in vain"!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:48.740
But...

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:56.580
It really gets my blood pumping
when we're swarmed with customers.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.080
YEAH

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:01.670
Thanks to all the people who stopped by,
we sold lots of our usual sweets too.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:05.220
I guess a loss leader is fine
when it comes to attracting customers.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:10.470
It's like when you go to the supermarket
if they have milk on sale for 128 yen, right?

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:15.770
Or 100 grams of ham for 68 yen
or a can of tomatoes for 78 yen.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:18.650
But of course you buy other stuff
while you're there, right?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:28.950
Your mom and grandma
were both natural salesladies.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:33.080
Whether they'd make something
sweet or sour, it didn't matter.

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.080
There'd always be a line of people.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:40.290
It was really something.
I thought that every time there was a festival.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:42.670
I wish you girls would've seen it, too.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:44.170
GLOW

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:48.050
I remember.
The deep-fried kitty-cats and lanterns.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.430
The bags with the huge ribbons were so cute.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:56.940
They often said,
"Spend effort, not money."

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.440
I'd help out by stuffing the bags.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.780
It was so much fun.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:08.490
You did a great job for your first time out there.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.950
But you still need to work on sales and have
a ways to go with finesse and insight.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:17.580
But you can give it
another shot next year, if you want.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.580
What? Really? Is it okay?

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.580
I'll do my best!

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.580
FWOHHH

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:25.090
I'll have customers lined up,
just like Mom and Grandma did!

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.970
OHHH

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.920
I need to think about the menu right away!

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:27.920
STRETCH

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.300
FWOHHH

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.800
Hina! Calm down.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.800
GRAB

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.930
You have entrance exams first.
Which schools are you applying to?

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.310
Oh yeah.

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:36.430
That's right.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:39.940
You have the summer term test tomorrow.
Despite the summer vacation, it's a school day.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.190
Did you study for the test?

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:47.240
Uh, yeah, I did.
I still have to study a little more though.

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.200
I've got it, Sis, how about jelly?

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.070
Hey!

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:59.210
CRESCENT MOON

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:53.660
Your hands have stopped!

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:56.450
Wrap it already!
The red bean pancake will dry out!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:59.210
Right! Sorry, Grandpa!

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:04.960
I can't!

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.340
I-I-I can't do it!

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.220
SHAKE
SHAKE

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.220
SHIVER
SHIVER

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:09.220
I just can't do it!

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:12.800
It's impossible!
I can't be the homeroom teacher for 3A!

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:16.930
It'll be fine, fine.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:18.430
Maybe.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.560
I'll be here if you need me.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:23.060
PANIC

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:22.730
It's too much to bear!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:25.320
You saw it, too!
The menacing look of Takagi's mother!

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:28.820
I-I don't have the confidence
to contend with her!

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:31.150
<i>What? What?!</i>

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.450
<i>A new homeroom teacher?</i>

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:39.450
<i>You're entrusting the precious last semester
of the third year to a young teacher like that?!</i>

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.460
<i>What is the school thinking?!</i>

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:46.340
WAHHH

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.340
I can't do it! I'm still a newbie!

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.340
You may be a newbie, but I'm an old man!

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:53.340
I can't physically be
the homeroom teacher for two classes!

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.970
I can't watch 90 students by myself!

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.350
On top of that, I've got my duties
as the head teacher!

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:04.850
Besides, how long will this
ongoing discussion with Takagi last?

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:12.110
I told you. Getting her
to understand what she did is part of the job.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:18.370
With all due respect, no matter what else
we say to her, it won't do any good.

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:23.620
She's already decided
not to feel any guilt over it.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.790
Why do we have to spend all this time on it?

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:28.500
It doesn't make sense.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:33.720
Paying all this attention
to the person who caused the trouble,

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:37.390
while the victim, Chiho Sakura,
not only moved away because of it,

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:40.680
but she isn't going to school yet over there.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:49.020
I-If she's unwilling to give in,
even if there was no malice...

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:52.070
I mean, after taking it this far,

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:55.320
it doesn't matter if there was ill will or not!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:57.320
Komigawa.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.950
I'll write it on her record.

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:03.580
As her new homeroom teacher,
I'll write it all down.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:08.380
That she thinks she's always right
and is very aggressive towards other people.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:14.340
That she's like the leader of the group,
but causes major problems in class.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:15.550
And!

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:20.720
When somebody causes a problem,
they need to take responsibility for it.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.890
That's what I believe.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:24.980
There must be punishment.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.350
Otherwise...

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.730
that's wrong, isn't it?

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.210
Hey, Mr. Kokubu.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:52.710
Do you have an answer?

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:58.470
Did you find a reason for why everyone
has to put out effort and do their best?

00:18:59.180 --> 00:19:00.550
Did you find something?

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:04.810
Well. I've been thinking a lot since it came up.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.730
And...

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.190
I couldn't find an answer.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.500
You didn't find it?

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.120
What the heck?

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:32.540
ATTENDANCE
RECORDS

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:35.550
I racked my brains, but in the end,
to be honest, I came up blank.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:38.510
It's strange, isn't it?

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:45.020
And when I thought about it,
I realized I never even had any doubts about it.

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.020
Why was that?

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:54.150
It's hard to make an effort,
but I always assumed people had to do it.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:20:01.280
All this time I thought making an effort
was something you do for your own sake.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:06.910
Anyway, I'd been told that often enough

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:12.040
that I don't even remember
who first said it or where I'd read that idea.

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:15.840
Now that I've reached this age,

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:20.260
I felt that phrase was true
from the bottom of my heart.

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:24.140
For the longest time, I probably just...

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:31.440
wanted to become a better person
than I was back then.

00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:37.320
So we're suddenly talking about you?

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.570
Is it going to take long?

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:44.070
No.

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:46.160
Time's up.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:50.330
This was my last day
as your class's interim homeroom teacher.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.750
Hey, Takagi.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:58.210
Right now, I think you have a lot of anxiety
that you don't know what to do.

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:04.090
You haven't done anything in your life yet,
so you don't know your own capabilities.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.970
That's the cause of your anxiety.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.350
Mr. Kokubu.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:14.100
You refuse to make an effort with anything

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:17.940
because you're scared of learning your own
capacity and being disappointed by it.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:22.450
But Takagi...

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.740
It's okay to be disappointed.

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:29.870
Once you learn your own capacity, you at last
understand what it is you should do.

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:33.000
When you understand yourself,

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:37.880
what you want to do
will also become more clear.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:44.880
Once you do that, you'll at least be able
to get past your incredible anxiety.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:50.060
I can guarantee at least that.

00:21:56.230 --> 00:22:00.940
<i>After I was done with the test,
that night, I made a lot of drawings.</i>

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:08.070
<i>There were so many colorful sweets swimming
around in my head and they wouldn't stop.</i>

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:15.000
Hina, how long are you going to stay up?

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:16.710
Take your bath.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:19.420
Hey, don't just leave the fan on.

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:21.380
Sheesh, you'll catch a cold.

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:25.260
Oh, Hina.

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:30.930
Geez. What is all this?

00:22:37.230 --> 00:22:40.150
My, my. What is this?

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:46.530
Cute.

00:22:47.490 --> 00:22:50.030
They all look delicious.

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:53.910
Yeah. These are great.

00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:56.000
I'm getting excited!

00:22:57.290 --> 00:23:00.040
Summer Vacation (Part 1)

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.470
Episode 42

00:24:32.390 --> 00:24:35.510
They're beautiful and look delicious.

00:24:35.510 --> 00:24:37.470
Rei, how old were you
when you first

00:24:37.470 --> 00:24:39.600
wanted to become
a professional shogi player?

00:24:39.600 --> 00:24:43.270
Kiriyama! It's a beautiful day, isn't it?

00:24:43.270 --> 00:24:45.820
I like smooth stuff!

00:24:47.070 --> 00:24:50.030
That's really adorable!

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
AKIMAN

00:24:51.150 --> 00:24:53.820
Grandpa, look at the sweets
Hina thought up!

00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:57.370
These are great!
